====================================================================================================
MSRE fuel salt property verification -- Phase 1
====================================================================================================

Scope.  Arithmetic and unit-conversion verification of the four correlations in
MSRE.Media.FuelSalt.Utilities, plus a like-for-like comparison against the MSRE
fuel salt medium TRANSFORM itself ships.  No measurement is involved, so nothing
below is an experimental validation.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1.  UNIT CONVERSIONS  (the documented imperial value <-> the SI constant in the code)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[PASS] cp: 0.47 Btu/(lb.degF) -> J/(kg.K) vs coded 1967     got        1967.8 J/(kg.K)   expected          1967  rel  4.05e-04 (tol 5e-04)
         0.47 x 4186.8 = 1967.80; the code rounds to 1967, i.e. -0.041 %.
[PASS] k: coded 1.44 W/(m.K) -> Btu/(hr.ft.degF)            got      0.832016 Btu/(hr.ft.degF) expected         0.832  rel  1.98e-05 (tol 1e-03)
         1.44 / 1.730735 = 0.83202 Btu/(hr.ft.degF).
[NOTE] lambda_T.mo's docstring says 0.83 Btu/(hr.ft.degF), which converts to 1.43651 W/(m.K),
       not the coded 1.44 (-0.24 %). The docstring is a rounded restatement, not the provenance
       of the constant.
[PASS] 1200 degF -> K (the docstring's reference point)     got       922.039 K          expected           922  rel  4.22e-05 (tol 1e-04)
         1200 degF = 922.039 K; the medium's reference_T is 922 K.
[PASS] mu(922 K) in cP vs the docstring's 7.6 cP            got       7.56508 cP         expected           7.6  rel  4.59e-03 (tol 1e-02)
         eta(922) = 7.56508e-03 Pa.s = 7.5651 cP.
[PASS] rho(922 K) with the correct degC argument            got       2242.14 kg/m3      expected       2242.14  rel  2.23e-08 (tol 1e-04)
         Reading the same correlation with a kelvin argument would give 2102.0 kg/m3, -6.2 %. This is why d_T.mo subtracts 273.15: the correlation is stated in degC.

